    "result": "I implemented `add_business_days` in `solution.py`, keeping the stub's signature, and wrote 52 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes. The implementation handles all three cases in the spec: forward and backward movement with `start` never counted, and `n == 0` returning `start` or the next business day. Holidays are copied into a set up front, so generators work. Type checks reject `datetime` for `start` and for holiday elements, and reject `bool` and `float` for `n`. The tests cover weekends, consecutive and duplicate holidays, weekend holidays, large spans, return type, and every `TypeError` path. I did not run coverage, mutation, CRAP or bandit gates, so those remain unchecked.",
